WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
This is kanbanana. I keep it beside
whatever I’m working on.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
It brings my Claude Code and Codex
desktop work into one little window.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Up here: what’s running, what needs me,
and what’s ready to check.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
I can scroll through the replies
without losing track of things.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Each card gives me a short version
of what the agent reported.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Click a conversation to open it
in Claude or Codex.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
If something matters most, I star it.
It stays at the top.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Once I’ve looked at it, I click here
to mark it Dealt with.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.000
It leaves this list. A new request
will bring it back.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.000
And when I want the bigger picture,
I expand to Projects.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:46.000
The conversations stay separate,
but now they’re grouped by project.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:52.000
These little notes remind me
what I’m trying to get done.
